# issue-flow — close (`/iflow-close`)

Finish and land the focus issue: tests, optional version bump, tracking updates, commit, push, PR. This skill never deletes branches; that is `/iflow-cleanup`.

{% set iflow_step = "close" %}
{% include "skills/_invocation_forms.md.j2" %}

{% include "skills/_model_directive.md.j2" %}

{% include "skills/_resolve_project_root.md.j2" %}

## Input tokens

| Token | Effect |
|---|---|
| `bump` / `patch` / `minor` / `major` / `stable` / `alpha` / `beta` / `rc` / `post` / `dev` | Version bump (step 2). Natural language works too; ask once if unclear; never auto-pick `major`. |
| `nohistory` / `skip history` | Skip the changelog trailers (step 3). |
| `log "..."` / `note "..."` | Use this text as the changelog bullet. |
| `stay` / `stay on branch` / `don't switch` | Stay on the issue branch after the PR step. |
| `draft` | Open or keep a draft PR; skips the `yolo` merge. |
| `yolo` | Hands-off: decide the changelog without asking, merge the PR, switch back and pull. Used by `/iflow-run yolo`. |
| `ops` / `nopr` / `no-pr` | No PR. Read `ops.md` in this skill folder and follow it **instead of** the steps below. Cannot combine with `yolo` or `draft`; stop and ask if combined. |

## Side files (read only when the step needs them)

| File | When |
|---|---|
| `version.md` | Step 2: a bump was requested, or a `{{ publish_label }}` label is on the issue. |
| `changelog.md` | Step 3: composing the changelog trailers. |
| `sync.md` | Step 6: replaying the branch onto the default branch. |
| `merge.md` | Step 8a: the `yolo` token is present. |
| `ci.md` | You need to list or wait on CI with `gh`. |
| `ops.md` | The `ops` / `nopr` / `no-pr` token is present. |

## Steps

1. **Sanity check.** Run the project test suite (e.g. `uv run pytest`) and any checks the repo relies on.{%- include "skills/_essential_tests_close_sanity.md.j2" -%}{% if ruff_autofix %} If the project uses ruff, run `ruff check --fix` and `ruff format` through the project's runner before committing.{% endif %} Skim the diff and avoid bundling unrelated changes. Record any design decision from this issue under `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ designs_folder }}/`.{% if suggest_graphify %} After a large structural change, when `graphify-out/` exists, *suggest* `/iflow-status graph`.{% endif %}{% if "pstack_blast_radius" in included_skills %} For a small diff you do not fully trust, *suggest* the `blast-radius` skill.{% endif %}
{%- if essential_tests and essential_review in ("close", "both") %}

1a. **Essential tests review.**
{% include "skills/_essential_tests_review.md.j2" %}
{%- endif %}

2. **Version bump (optional).** When a bump was requested{% if label_flows %} or the issue carries a `{{ publish_label }}` label{% endif %}, read `version.md` and follow it. Run the bump from the project root after step 1 and before the commit.{% if confirm_version_bump %} Without `yolo`, when no bump was requested and there is no publish label, ask once whether to bump.{% endif %}

3. **Changelog trailers.** Unless `nohistory`, read `changelog.md` and put `Changelog`, `Changelog-Date`, and `Changelog-Id` trailers at the end of the commit message. **Never edit or stage `{{ history_file }}` on the issue branch.**{% if confirm_changelog_update %} Without `yolo`, show the bullet and confirm once; if declined, stop and offer revise / `nohistory` / abort.{% else %} Do not ask for confirmation.{% endif %} Do this even when an early draft PR exists. Never offer a changelog update after close has finished or after merge.

4. **Issue tracking.** Update `issue<N>_status.md` (what is done, what remains). Tick `- [x] Done` only when fully resolved. Then move the `issue<N>_*` group to `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ solved_folder }}/` (done) or `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ partly_solved_folder }}/` (not done).

5. **Commit.** Check `git status`. If any change is not relevant to this issue, name it and ask whether to include it. Stage intentionally (include `pyproject.toml` / `uv.lock` after a bump). Write the message in full sentences: what changed and why.

6. **Sync with the default branch.** Run `issue-flow agent sync-branch --json`. It replays the branch onto `origin/<default>` and resolves additive bookkeeping conflicts. On exit 1, report its `notes` and **stop**. Read `sync.md` for stacked branches or when the CLI is missing.

7. **Push.** Push to `origin`. When step 6 rewrote the branch (`needs_force_push: true`), use `git push --force-with-lease`. Never a bare `--force`; never against the default branch.

8. **Pull request.** Always pass `--repo <owner/repo>`.
   - Run `gh pr list --repo <owner/repo> --head <branch> --state open --json number,url,isDraft` first. Update an existing PR (including an early draft) instead of opening a second one.
   - Else `gh pr create` (`--draft` with the `draft` token). The body explains the change, how to test it, and links the issue (`Closes #N`).
   - When the PR is a draft and the user did not pass `draft`, run `gh pr ready <number> --repo <owner/repo>`.
   - Report a one-shot `gh pr checks <number> --repo <owner/repo>` snapshot. Offer `issue-flow agent pr-ready <number> --watch` when the user wants to wait; do not run it unasked.
{% include "skills/_gh_body_file.md.j2" %}
{% if "pstack_unslop" in included_skills %}   - *Offer* the `unslop` skill for the PR body (skip under `yolo`).
{% endif %}

8a. **Merge (`yolo` only).** Read `merge.md` and follow it. Without `yolo`, merging is the user's decision.

9. **Switch back.**{% if not auto_switchback %} `auto_switchback = false`: stay on the issue branch unless the user asks to switch.{% else %} Unless `stay` was passed, run `issue-flow agent switchback --json` after the PR step (after the merge with `yolo`). It refuses on a dirty tree, switches home to the default branch, and runs `git pull --ff-only`. In a linked worktree (`in_worktree: true`) it skips the switch; pull from home with `-C <home>`. On exit 1, report its notes and stop.

{% include "skills/_default_sync_recover.md.j2" %}{% endif %}

9a. **Remove the issue worktree.** {% include "skills/_worktree_close_remove.md.j2" %}

10. **After review.** Without `yolo`, address feedback, push, and merge when approved and checks are green.{% if auto_cleanup %} `auto_cleanup = true`: once the PR is `MERGED`, follow the `iflow-cleanup` skill. If still open after a `gh pr checks --watch --fail-fast` of at most {{ checks_watch_minutes }} minutes, stop and report. Never merge because of this knob.{% elif remind_cleanup %} Remind the user to run `/iflow-cleanup` once the PR has merged. Do not run it from here.{% endif %}

11. **Output.** Commit, push result, PR URL, final branch, worktree removal, merge result (with `yolo`), and the next step. When `epic_session.md` exists, hint `/iflow` for the next epic child.

## Constraints

- Do not skip failing tests without the user's explicit agreement.
- Never delete branches here. Never `gh pr merge --admin`, never skip CI, never force-push anything but the issue branch (`--force-with-lease`).
- Only additive bookkeeping conflicts are resolved automatically (step 6). Every other conflict stops the flow.
- The `ops` token never opens a PR.
